        "problem": "Find $\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & a & b & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|$ given that $\\,|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|=8.$",
        "worked_solution": "Notice that we have a block upper triangular matrix. Therefore, its determinant is equal to the product of the diagonal blocks' determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & a & b & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & a & b & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =2\\cdot 8\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
